@startuml did-resolution-sequence
title Canton Network DID Standard - Resolution and Service Discovery (Informative)

actor "External Application" as App
participant "Bootstrap / Trust\nConfiguration" as Bootstrap
participant "DID Resolver" as Resolver
participant "Party Binding Proof /\nRegistry (Option B)" as Binding
participant "Additional Resolver(s)" as Other
participant "Credential or Asset\nRegistry API" as Service

App -> Bootstrap: Obtain resolver and trust-anchor configuration
Bootstrap --> App: Authenticated source identities and policy
App -> Resolver: Resolve DID (optionally requested version)
Resolver --> App: DID Document + state/version + verification evidence
App -> App: Verify source, integrity, canonical version,\nfreshness/finality, and deactivation status

opt Option B: verify current Party ID binding
  App -> Binding: Obtain binding proof or registry record
  Binding --> App: Party ID binding + status/version + evidence
  App -> App: Verify binding authority, integrity, currency,\nauthorization, revocation, and historical applicability
end

opt Additional multi-endpoint comparison policy
  note over App,Other
    Separate client policy, not inherent BFT.
    A BFT claim also needs independent sources,
    authenticated identities, canonical state/version,
    quorum/fault model, freshness/finality, and failure behavior.
  end note
  App -> Other: Resolve the same DID/version
  Other --> App: Additional result and evidence
  App -> App: Compare under explicit policy
end

App -> App: Select service by understood type and endpoint version
App -> Service: Invoke service-specific API
Service -> Service: Authenticate and authorize independently
Service --> App: API response
@enduml
